_LV=6.0.0`) rather than relying on the truncated log, then reverted the two test-result files that run accidentally touched.\n\n**What actually fails:** 2 of 8 tests — the ones that boot a real `AnnotationConfigApplicationContext` with `@EnableSpringConfigured` or `@EnableTransactionManagement/@EnableCaching/@EnableAsync(mode = AdviceMode.ASPECTJ)` — throw `com.oracle.svm.core.jdk.UnsupportedFeatureError: Classes cannot be defined at runtime`, from `org.springframework.cglib.core.ReflectUtils.defineClass`. Tracing into spring-aspects 6.0.0 sources, `SpringConfiguredConfiguration` and `AspectJTransactionManagementConfiguration` are plain `@Configuration` classes (default `proxyBeanMethods = true`), which Spring's `ConfigurationClassPostProcessor.enhanceConfigurationClasses` unconditionally CGLIB-enhances via runtime bytecode generation — there's no `NativeDetector`/property bypass in 6.0.0's `ConfigurationClassPostProcessor`/`ConfigurationClassUtils`. The only known workaround (native-image agent's predefined-classes support) is explicitly banned by this repo's contract (`predefined-classes-config.json` is a rejected legacy format).\n\nHowever, this is **not** a whole-library blocker: the other 6/8 tests, which call `AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect.aspectOf()` / `GenericInterfaceDrivenDependencyInjectionAspect` etc. directly without booting a full `ApplicationContext`, pass cleanly in native image. There's a viable fallback (drive the aspects directly rather than through Spring's `@Enable*` + `AnnotationConfigApplicationContext` path), so per the SOLE PATH criterion this doesn't qualify as unsupportable — it's repairable by scoping the generated tests away from that specific CGLIB-triggering flow. No extra Maven dependency, Docker image, or env/system property is needed; `spring-context`, `spring-tx`, and `assertj-core` are already declared and resolve fine.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"No extra dependency/Docker/env setup needed; flag that Spring-context-driven @Enable*(mode=ASPECTJ)/@EnableSpringConfigured flows CGLIB-enhance library-internal @Configuration classes at runtime and must be avoided in generated tests.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Do not exercise @EnableSpringConfigured, @EnableTransactionManagement(mode = AdviceMode.ASPECTJ), @EnableCaching(mode = AdviceMode.ASPECTJ), or @EnableAsync(mode = AdviceMode.ASPECTJ) through a real AnnotationConfigApplicationContext.refresh(). Spring's ConfigurationClassPostProcessor unconditionally CGLIB-enhances the library's own internal full @Configuration classes (org.springframework.context.annotation.aspectj.SpringConfiguredConfiguration, org.springframework.transaction.aspectj.AspectJTransactionManagementConfiguration, and the equivalent cache/async ones), which calls org.springframework.cglib.core.ReflectUtils.defineClass at runtime and fails under Native Image with UnsupportedFeatureError (verified locally against 6.0.0 with GVM_TCK_LV=6.0.0 GVM_TCK_NATIVE_IMAGE_MODE=current-defaults). This repo's reachability-metadata.json format has no predefined-classes support to register that runtime-defined class, so there is no metadata fix. Instead, cover these aspects the way the existing 5.3.31 suite already does for its passing tests: obtain the aspect via its static aspectOf() accessor (AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect.aspectOf(), AnnotationTransactionAspect.aspectOf(), AnnotationCacheAspect.aspectOf(), AnnotationAsyncExecutionAspect.aspectOf()) and configure/invoke it directly, or use GenericInterfaceDrivenDependencyInjectionAspect directly, instead of booting a full ApplicationContext through the @Enable* annotations.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Avoiding the ApplicationContext-driven @Enable*(mode=ASPECTJ)/@EnableSpringConfigured flow means the generated test won't cover Spring's bean-registration/@Configuration integration path of spring-aspects, only the direct aspectOf()-based usage — this is an inherent Native Image limitation (runtime CGLIB class definition) with no metadata-based fix available in this repo's format, not a scaffold or dependency gap.\",\n    \"This CGLIB/@Configuration enhancement issue is likely generic to other Spring modules tested under the current stricter native-image default mode, not unique to spring-aspects 6.0.0 — worth flagging if similar failures show up on other spring-* version bumps.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":4103,"type":"result","duration_ms":348693,"uuid":"5bae256d-ed05-4089-9011-3152e3ec5f12","ttft_stream_ms":1122,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":1123,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

